# Runbook: Enable RDMA on SR-IOV VFs (OpenShift)

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Runbook ID | RB-SRIOV-RDMA-001 |
| Cluster | lab4.srib-lab-ocp.lan (master1/2/3, control-plane + worker) |
| Platform | OpenShift 4.14 / 4.18, SR-IOV Network Operator |
| Hardware | Intel E810, vendor `8086`, device `1593`, driver `ice`, 25 GbE |
| Target PF | `ens1f2` (PCI `0000:11:00.2`) – VFs 9–12 |
| Change type | Node configuration change – possible drain/reboot |
| Estimated duration | 60–90 min (including node sync) |
| Risk | Medium – shared PF with existing BPP/BIP VF groups |
| Rollback time | ~15 min |

---

## 1. Purpose

Enable RoCEv2 RDMA on a dedicated group of SR-IOV virtual functions so that RDMA-capable workloads (AI/GPU training, MPI, NVMe-oF, RDMA storage) can be scheduled on the cluster, without affecting the existing BPP (`vfio-pci`) and BIP (`netdevice`) VF groups.

## 2. Scope

**In scope**
- New `SriovNetworkNodePolicy` with `isRdma: true` on `ens1f2` VFs 9–12
- New `SriovNetwork` and resulting NetworkAttachmentDefinition
- Functional validation with `perftest`

**Out of scope**
- Switch PFC/ECN configuration (prerequisite, owned by network team)
- Changing `rdmaMode` from `shared` to `exclusive`
- Any change to existing policies `policy-ens1f2-bh0u`, `policy-ens1f2-bh0c`, or other PFs

## 3. Roles

| Role | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Change executor | Runs all `oc` steps, owns validation and rollback |
| Network team | Confirms PFC/ECN/VLAN on switch ports before start |
| Application owner | Provides RDMA test image, confirms workload expectations |
| Approver | Approves change window and go/no-go after pre-checks |

