## 5. Change procedure

### 5.1 Create target namespace

```bash
oc new-project rdma-app
```

### 5.2 Apply RDMA node policy

`sriov-rdma-node-policy.yaml`:

```yaml
apiVersion: sriovnetwork.openshift.io/v1
kind: SriovNetworkNodePolicy
metadata:
  name: policy-ens1f2-rdma
  namespace: openshift-sriov-network-operator
spec:
  resourceName: rdma_sriov_net
  nodeSelector:
    feature.node.kubernetes.io/network-sriov.capable: "true"
  priority: 99
  numVfs: 16
  nicSelector:
    vendor: "8086"
    deviceID: "1593"
    pfNames: ["ens1f2#9-12"]
  deviceType: netdevice
  isRdma: true
  linkType: eth
```

```bash
oc apply -f sriov-rdma-node-policy.yaml
```

Expected:

```
sriovnetworknodepolicy.sriovnetwork.openshift.io/policy-ens1f2-rdma created
```

If the webhook rejects the policy, stop and check Section 8.

### 5.3 Monitor node sync

```bash
watch oc get sriovnetworknodestates -n openshift-sriov-network-operator
```

Nodes move `Idle → Drain_Required → Draining → InProgress → Idle` one at a time. Wait until all three show:

```
NAME                            SYNC STATUS   DESIRED SYNC STATE   CURRENT SYNC STATE
master1.lab4.srib-lab-ocp.lan   Succeeded     Idle                 Idle
master2.lab4.srib-lab-ocp.lan   Succeeded     Idle                 Idle
master3.lab4.srib-lab-ocp.lan   Succeeded     Idle                 Idle
```

If a node reboots, watch its console and wait for `Ready` before continuing. Do not apply further changes while any node is not `Idle`.

### 5.4 Confirm resource advertised

```bash
oc describe nodes | grep rdma_sriov_net
```

Expected on each node:

```
openshift.io/rdma_sriov_net:   4
```

### 5.5 Confirm VF binding on a node

```bash
ssh core@master1.lab4.srib-lab-ocp.lan
ip link show ens1f2 | grep -E "vf (9|10|11|12) "
rdma link show
lsmod | grep irdma
exit
```

Expected: `rdma link show` lists one `rocep17s0f2v<N>` device per RDMA VF with `state ACTIVE`.

### 5.6 Apply SriovNetwork

`sriov-rdma-network.yaml`:

```yaml
apiVersion: sriovnetwork.openshift.io/v1
kind: SriovNetwork
metadata:
  name: rdma-net
  namespace: openshift-sriov-network-operator
spec:
  resourceName: rdma_sriov_net
  networkNamespace: rdma-app
  vlan: <VLAN_ID>          # remove this line if the RoCE network is untagged
  spoofChk: "off"
  trust: "on"
  ipam: |
    {
      "type": "whereabouts",
      "range": "192.168.30.0/24",
      "exclude": ["192.168.30.1/32"]
    }
```

```bash
oc apply -f sriov-rdma-network.yaml
oc get net-attach-def -n rdma-app
```

Expected:

```
NAME       AGE
rdma-net   5s
```

