## 6. Validation

### 6.1 Deploy test pods on two nodes

`rdma-test-pod.yaml` (deploy twice, changing `name` and `nodeName`):

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: rdma-test-1
  namespace: rdma-app
  annotations:
    k8s.v1.cni.cncf.io/networks: rdma-net
spec:
  nodeName: master1.lab4.srib-lab-ocp.lan
  containers:
  - name: perftest
    image: <registry>/rdma-perftest:latest
    command: ["sleep", "infinity"]
    securityContext:
      capabilities:
        add: ["IPC_LOCK"]
    resources:
      requests:
        openshift.io/rdma_sriov_net: "1"
        cpu: "2"
        memory: "4Gi"
      limits:
        openshift.io/rdma_sriov_net: "1"
        cpu: "2"
        memory: "4Gi"
```

```bash
oc apply -f rdma-test-pod.yaml          # rdma-test-1 on master1
oc apply -f rdma-test-pod-2.yaml        # rdma-test-2 on master2
oc get pod -n rdma-app -o wide
```

- [ ] Both pods `Running`

### 6.2 Device visible in pod

```bash
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test-1 -- ls /dev/infiniband
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test-1 -- ibv_devinfo
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test-1 -- ip -4 addr show net1
```

- [ ] `uverbs0` and `rdma_cm` present
- [ ] `ibv_devinfo` shows `state: PORT_ACTIVE`, `link_layer: Ethernet`
- [ ] `net1` has an IP from the whereabouts range

Record device name (`<DEV>`) and IP of each pod.

### 6.3 Connectivity

```bash
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test-1 -- ping -c 3 <IP_OF_POD_2>
```

- [ ] Ping succeeds

### 6.4 RDMA bandwidth

Terminal 1 (server):

```bash
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test-2 -- ib_write_bw -d <DEV> -F --report_gbits
```

Terminal 2 (client):

```bash
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test-1 -- ib_write_bw -d <DEV> -F --report_gbits <IP_OF_POD_2>
```

- [ ] Average bandwidth ≥ 20 Gb/s on 25 GbE

### 6.5 RDMA latency

```bash
# server
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test-2 -- ib_write_lat -d <DEV> -F
# client
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test-1 -- ib_write_lat -d <DEV> -F <IP_OF_POD_2>
```

- [ ] Typical latency ≤ 10 µs

### 6.6 Multi-stream (PFC check)

```bash
# server
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test-2 -- ib_write_bw -d <DEV> -F --report_gbits -q 8
# client
oc exec -n rdma-app rdma-test-1 -- ib_write_bw -d <DEV> -F --report_gbits -q 8 <IP_OF_POD_2>
```

- [ ] Aggregate bandwidth stays ≥ 20 Gb/s (a sharp drop indicates PFC not active on the switch)

### 6.7 Regression check on existing VF groups

```bash
oc describe nodes | grep pci_sriov
oc get pods -A -o wide | grep -E "<existing-sriov-app-namespace>"
```

- [ ] `pci_sriov_net_bh0u` = 4 and `pci_sriov_net_bh0c` = 5 on every node (unchanged)
- [ ] Existing BPP/BIP pods `Running` and passing their own health checks

### 6.8 Cleanup test pods

```bash
oc delete pod rdma-test-1 rdma-test-2 -n rdma-app
```

